{
  "_doc": "Colors are Endesga 32 palette indexes. accent = [dark, mid, light] tints tiles, sky and creatures. The first planet is the default start. intro: 'scan' (the homeworld's opening: Thales finishes copying himself and wakes you, src/data/homeworld.json) or 'land' (the ship descends). ground = [dark, base, speckle] floor colors (default [25, 24, 23]). dayCycle: lighting follows the device clock (src/data/daycycle.json). weather: real-hour rain. ponds: number of ponds. flowers: chance per open tile. wildlife: peaceful creatures (grazers can be petted). poles: polar caps seen from orbit (size 0..1 from equator to pole, [edge, core] palette colors); leave out for none. shy: the world's creatures never attack; they flee from you (Earth is peaceful: humanity is gone, nature took the ruins back). On every world creatures leave you alone in the town (enemies.json townSafe). gravity: surface gravity in Earth g (heavier worlds shorten the dash, make dust fall faster and landings heavier). sunTint: multiplies the day cycle's light and sky (a red dwarf's dim red day); the tint is the sun's, so it fades as the night comes and the night keeps only a share of it (light.json nightSun). wildCems: fields of wild Cems lying in the salt (the Cems' world, Gliese 12 b; src/entities/WildCems.ts): how many fields, Cems per field [min, max], and salt blooms around each (saved as nodes wild0, wild1, ...). lacks: materials the world has no nodes of (the homeworld gave its copper and quartz to the founding, story/STORY.md The beginning); the ship's hold brings them (supplies.json signature.lacksHold).",
